# A hand bears what its arm can: a weapon too heavy for it is held, not wielded.
#
# --weapons puts an arming sword (medium) in the right hand and a round shield (medium) in the left,
# and lifts each arm to level 1 so the loadout can be fought with. --organs arms=0 is applied after
# that and wins, so both arms are left at 0 — which bears light things only (PartyMember.HoldLimit).
# The sword stays in the right hand, and the Bellic tab, which reads exactly what the fight reads
# (PartyMember.WieldedWeapons), calls it too heavy and offers no long blade block. The hunting bow
# is light, so the weak left arm that ended up with it still wields it: the bar is the weight.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --weapons --organs arms=0 --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --period noon

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 45

manage Bellic
wait 1
expect too heavy
expect-not long blade
expect bow, left hand, lv 4
dump

quit
